This is a timeline of events that occurred in '''2015'''.

==2015==
*[[William Rawlins]] becomes Director of Covert Affairs at the [[CIA]].{{Ref|TP108}}
*[[Dinah Madani]] returns from [[Kandahar]] to the [[United States]] after a 3-year mission in which her partner, [[Ahmad Zubair]], ended up killed.{{Ref|TP109}}
*''Walking the Nile'' is published by {{WPS|Levison Wood}}.{{Ref|RealEvents}}{{Ref|MK101}}
*[[Helen Cho]] prepares a speech on her [[Regeneration Cradle]]. She prepares to follow in the footsteps of [[Maya Hansen]] and [[John F. Burke]].{{Ref|TWFATEotAaB}}

===January===
*[[Alex Bellamy]] dies.<ref name="Bellamy">[[:File:Alex Bellamy Gravestone BTS.jpg|Alex Bellamy Gravestone]]</ref>{{Ref|SMBND}}
*[[Vanessa Marianna]] is taken to [[Felix Manning]], a fixer working for [[Wilson Fisk]], for protection and help staying hidden.{{Ref|DD312}}<ref>In ''[[One Last Shot]]'', in October 2017 (see [[2017]] references), Wilson Fisk says to Felix Manning, "You protected her... two years. You kept Vanessa safe when I couldn't." This would suggest Manning began his oversight of Marianna around 2015. This likely would've began shortly after Fisk's arrest, however, which occurred on December 16, 2014 (see [[2014]] references). With this in mind, it can be taken that Manning's protection of Marianna began around January 2015, a few short weeks after Fisk's arrest and two calendar years before the events of ''One Last Shot''.</ref>

====5th====
*[[Sana Ali]] loses her dog, [[Magnum]]. Once she finds him, she has him microchipped to avoid losing him again.{{Ref|MM105}}<ref>In ''[[Time and Again]]'', Sana Ali says on October 10, 2025 (see [[2025]] references) that she had her dog microchipped. This could have happened between then and when Muneeba Khan left home in April 2004 (see [[2000s]] references), since Khan seems not to know about the incident. It can therefore be approximated that Magnum got lost on the midpoint of these dates, January 2015.</ref>
*[[Pym Technologies]] posts on {{WPS|Google+}} saying "''[[Hope van Dyne]] leads team of new scientists on a special project. CEO [[Darren Cross]] to oversee the management. More information to come later.''"<ref name="PT G+"/>{{Ref|AM}}<ref name="Social Media"/>

====11th====
*'''[[Infiltration into Gabriel Soto's Mansion]]''': The month after the fire in the church, thanks to [[Skye]], Coulson and [[Melinda May]] manage to infiltrate the event to recover the painting with the aliens drawings.{{Ref|AoS204}}<ref name="AoS2 Stretching">''[[Shadows]]'' and ''[[Heavy Is the Head]]'' occur in June 2014 (see other references), but ''[[A Fractured House]]'' has to take place no earlier than March 2015 (see [[2015]] references). There are undetermined spans of time between ''Heavy is the Head'' and ''[[Making Friends and Influencing People]]'', ''Making Friends and Influencing People'' and ''[[Face My Enemy]]'', and a mostly undetermined span between ''[[A Hen in the Wolf House]]'' and ''A Fractured House'' other than that when ''A Fractured House'' picks up, it does not seem that Morse and Hunter have been reunited for long. A weighted distribution of these episodes' events places 107 days between the events of ''Heavy is the Head'' and ''Making Friends and Influencing People'', a further 107 days between ''Making Friends and Influencing People'' and ''Face My Enemy'', and 53 days between ''A Hen in the Wolf House'' and ''A Fractured House'' to stretch the first set of episodes to fill out the span of time reasonably. This finally places ''Making Friends and Influencing People'' on September 24-26, 2014 and ''Face My Enemy'' and ''A Hen in the Wolf House'' from January 11-14, 2015. This fits well with a statement from Brett Dalton, [https://tvline.com/casting-news/agents-of-shield-skye-ward-shooting-spoilers-580061/ <nowiki>saying, "Ward had a hell of a time in the cage by himself for 6 months [until] he makes a promise; to reunite Skye with her dad,"</nowiki>] which refers to the events of ''Making Friends and Influencing People''. With that episode being September 2014, this works nicely as 6 months after March 2014.</ref><ref name="AoS2 May Talks at Party">In ''[[Face My Enemy]]'', Skye jokingly states that "[May] just said more words than I've heard her say in a year", implying that she has known May for over a year. The reasoned date for her saying this is January 11, 2015, and the reasoned date for her first meeting May is September 9, 2013, which works.</ref>
*'''[[Ambush at the Hotel La Ona]]''':
**[[File:Fme4.png|250px|thumb|May fighting Agent 33]][[Hydra]] agents, [[Sunil Bakshi]] (disguised as [[Glenn Talbot]]), and [[Agent 33]] (disguised as Melinda May) attack Coulson, also looking for the painting.{{Ref|AoS204}}
**May helps Coulson, and electrocutes Agent 33's face, causing damage to her [[Photostatic Veil]], rendering it permanently stuck to her face looking like May, with a burn mark. Coulson leaves Bakshi unconscious, then he and May steal the painting, which was in possession of Hydra.{{Ref|AoS204}}
*Coulson tells May that if his urges to draw the extraterrestrial symbols, the "[[Words of Creation]]", ever make him as crazy as [[John Garrett]] became, she needs to kill him.{{Ref|AoS204}}
*'''[[Massacre at the Wedding Party]]''': [[Hydra]] agents infiltrate the wedding of [[Pete Leitner|Peter]] and [[Mariah Leitner]] and spike the champagne with a chemical based on the effects of the [[Obelisk]]. Nine people were killed as a result.{{Ref|AoS205}}

====12th====
*[[Raina]], reading a newspaper about the incident at the Hotel La Ona and trying to take a plane to Florida, is located by [[Daniel Whitehall]]. Whitehall tells her that if she does not give him the Obelisk within the next 48 hours, she will be tortured horribly, for a very long time.{{Ref|AoS204}}<ref name="AoS2 48 Hours Obelisk">In ''[[Face My Enemy]]'', Whitehall gives Raina "48 hours" to retrieve the Obelisk. The reasoned date for this is January 12th, making her deadline the morning of January 14th.</ref>
*Bakshi orders [[Jemma Simmons]] and [[Kenneth Turgeon]] to attend a meeting [[Daniel Whitehall]] was having with his top scientists, including Dr. [[Lingenfelter]]. Simmons explains that she has skin samples from a [[List of Minor Characters/Marvel Heroes#Heavy is the Head|waitress]] who had been petrified, but she could not duplicate the powers completely. Whitehall asks for suggestions from Simmons, to Turgeon's jealousy. Simmons then sends a secret message via [[Flex Screen]] to [[S.H.I.E.L.D.]]{{Ref|AoS205}}
*Sunil Bakshi and [[Bobbi Morse]], head of security at Hydra, discover there is a mole in the facility.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*[[File:Hen6.jpg|thumb|250px|Morse confronts Simmons]]Morse interrogates Simmons as Turgeon is dragged off, since a Flex Screen was found in his desk.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*[[Phil Coulson]] has been scribbling the [[Words of Creation]] into his desk when the field agents enter, wondering what to do about the wedding incident. When [[Skye]] notices the scribbling, she questions Coulson's orders, until he presses her and she runs out.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*Skye is researching the Words, but is interrupted by [[Lance Hunter]], who tells her to consult [[Grant Ward]] on the subject. Ward desperately hopes that Skye was not carving the Words, as he tells her that [[John Garrett]] did it more and more after his infusion with [[GH.325]], as he became crazier and crazier. When Ward tells her that [[Raina]] was his source on information pertaining to [[Skye's Father]], Skye refuses to listen.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*[[Raina]] begs [[Skye's Father]] to let her borrow the [[Obelisk]], but he refuses. He tells her to beg Whitehall for her life instead.{{Ref|AoS205}}

====13th====
*Going to [[Hydra Laboratories]], Raina sees Simmons sending a message to [[S.H.I.E.L.D.]]. Seeing an opportunity to use it as blackmail, Raina calls Coulson for a meeting.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*At a restaurant, Coulson meets with Raina to find out what she wants, with Hunter, Skye, and [[Melinda May]] listening. She tells Coulson that she wants to take Skye to her father, or else she will perform a file transfer of her photograph that will blow Simmons' cover at Hydra.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*However, Coulson refuses her offer and the file is sent. Raina is stunned. Hunter [[Tracker|tags]] her and allows her to leave after she reveals the doctor's location.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*[[File:Battle Staves 2.png|250px|thumb|Morse fights Hydra Agents]]'''[[Escape from Hydra Laboratories]]''': With the file that Raina sent, all eyes are on [[Jemma Simmons]]. [[Sunil Bakshi]] sends a security team to retrieve her. When [[Bobbi Morse]] comes with her team, Simmons is trapped. However, Morse then pulls out [[Bobbi Morse's Battle Staves|her battle staves]] and fights the agents, protecting Simmons and revealing that she is an undercover S.H.I.E.L.D. agent. The two are pursued to the roof where they jump onto the awaiting cloaked [[Quinjet]], piloted by [[Antoine Triplett]], and make their escape.{{Ref|AoS205}}<ref name="AoS2 48 Hours Obelisk"/>
*Skye goes solo to her father's hideout and finds his picture before Coulson and the others can catch her. When she sees the bodies of two of his patients on the floor, Skye calls him a monster. This upsets him as he watches on with cameras from his car nearby.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*Coulson welcomes Morse, Simmons, and Triplett when they arrive at the [[Playground]]. [[Leo Fitz]] is hesitant in greeting Simmons, and [[Alphonso Mackenzie]] is happy to see Morse. When Hunter sees Morse, he is upset that Coulson has him working with his ex-wife.{{Ref|AoS205}}
*Meanwhile, Skye wants full disclosure from Coulson about the writings, and he decides to give it. He tells her about his carvings, and she reveals to him that she believes the [[Words of Creation]] are a map.{{Ref|AoS205}}

====14th====
*[[File:ZaboGreetsWhitehall.jpg|thumb|250px|Calvin Zabo introduces himself to [[Daniel Whitehall]]]]Skye's father takes the [[Diviner]], as it is called in its native language, to [[Daniel Whitehall]]. He offers to teach him not only how to use its power, but how to survive it. When his motives are questioned, the doctor says that they share a common enemy: [[Phil Coulson]].{{Ref|AoS205}}<ref name="AoS2 Stretching"/><ref name="AoS2 Weeks of Work">In ''[[The Things We Bury]]'', Zabo says that he "could have saved [Whitehall] weeks of work" on the Diviner. Due to the necessary stretch between ''[[Heavy Is the Head]]'' and ''[[A Fractured House]]'', him taking the Diviner to Whitehall has to be in January, approximately 10 weeks before he says this on March 29th. This still fits, especially if Whitehall was not working on it immediately.</ref>

====17th====
