*Having now been on the planet for 851 hours, Simmons starts writhing on the floor, pretending to be poisoned so that the man will open the door to her cage and come in.{{Ref|AoS305}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/>
*[[File:TheChase4,722Hours.png|thumb|250px|Daniels pursues Simmons]]Simmons manage to trick him, hits him on the head with her food bowl and runs to escape, injuring herself in the process. The man catches up with her and grabs her, taking her back to his hideout to try and help her. He tells her that "It" can smell the blood and is coming. The man takes Simmons back underground to safety just before the sandstorm sweeps past, and he gives her medical instruments to sew up her wound, before revealing to her that he is called Will Daniels.{{Ref|AoS305}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/>
*Two hours later, the two start telling each other their stories. Simmons discovers that Daniels was an astronaut from [[NASA]], who arrived on the planet in 2001 and has been stranded there for the 14 years since. A little later, Daniels shows Simmons the maps he has drawn for the planet, and they talk about developments in technology.{{Ref|AoS305}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/>
*Daniels then starts telling the story of what happened to his team of astronauts in 2001 as they eat a meal together, saying that "It" caused his other three astronaut friends to go crazy and kill themselves, before attempting to kill him. All three of his friends are now dead because of It, but he has managed to avoid It all these years. Daniels and Simmons make a deal to work together to try to get home.{{Ref|AoS305}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/><ref name="Simmons Says It’s 2015">When Daniels asks, "What year is it?", Simmons replies, "2015", definitively giving the year.</ref>

====22nd====
*At the [[Avengers Compound]], [[Wanda Maximoff]] watches a sitcom and calls for [[Vision]] to enter. He phases in through the wall and apologizes for intruding. Maximoff asks Vision to sit next to her, and he obliges. They watch the sitcom, in which a character gets hurt. Vision asks what the joke is, and Maximoff explains he is not really injured since it is not that kind of show.<ref name="WV108 2015 Events">In ''[[Previously On]]'', a flashback is shown of Vision and Wanda Maximoff bonding for the first time in the New Avengers Compound. At the end of ''[[Avengers: Age of Ultron]]'' on June 21, 2015 (see other references), the Compound is shown to have finished construction. The flashback in ''Previously On'' shows Maximoff still mourning the loss of her brother, so it must be set close to the Battle of Sokovia. ''[[Marvel Studios' The Marvel Cinematic Universe: An Official Timeline]]'' places the scene after the June 21 scene, so it can be taken that this is shortly after (on another bad day for her) to allow it to still be close to her brother's death, making it approximately June 22, 2015.</ref>{{Ref|WV108}}
*Vision asks how she is feeling, and Maximoff asks why talking about her [[Pietro Maximoff|brother]]'s death would comfort her, claiming that seeing him is the only thing that would comfort her.<ref name="WV108 2015 Events"/>{{Ref|WV108}}
*[[File:WandaxVision.png|thumb|250px|[[Wanda Maximoff|Maximoff]] and [[Vision]] start to fall in love]] After an awkward silence, Maximoff apologizes and says that she is tired. She says that she is going to drown in her sorrow, but Vision says that it will not. Maximoff asks how Vision would know, and Vision explains that all he has ever known was being alone, and therefore has never experienced loss. However, he posits that grief is simply love persevering. Maximoff thinks about this as Vision laughs at the show they are watching. The two share in their enjoyment of the sitcom. They smile at each other and resume watching.<ref name="WV108 2015 Events"/>{{Ref|WV108}}

