*It's now been 3,010 hours (roughly 3 months) since [[Jemma Simmons]] arrived on the planet, and she is going crazy about wanting to get back home. She wants to go the "No Fly Zone" of the planet, but Daniels warns her that it is too dangerous, so instead Simmons goes out to find food for dinner. However, whilst she is out, she sees a sword in the ground in the distance and goes over to investigate. There Simmons finds the bones of everyone who has come to the planet in the past, and the belongings of one of these people from centuries ago, including a sextant for mapping the stars. She is suddenly caught in another sandstorm, and sees the dark, cloaked figure of "It" a little way away within the storm. Running for her life, she makes it back to her and Daniels' hideout just in time. Daniels tells her she had made a dangerous mistake and wandered into the No Fly Zone, but Simmons says that it does not matter now, as she has discovered a way for them to get home.{{Ref|AoS305}}{{Ref|AoS301}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/>

====20th====
*[[File:Maveth-Map.png|thumb|250px|Simmons identifies where she and Daniels arrived to Maveth]]Simmons explains to Daniels that the portal is fixed in place, but the planet they are on spins on its axis, therefore meaning the portal appears in different parts of the planet each time. She then explains that they can use her phone battery to power Daniels' NASA equipment and use the sextant to map the stars. Then they can use that data to calculate the speed at which the planet spins so that they can therefore work out where the portal will appear next.{{Ref|AoS305}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/>
*[[Joy Meachum]] hires [[Jessica Jones]] to find incriminating "dirt" on employees at Rand Enterprises, for future use.<ref name="IF1 Joy Jessica">In ''[[The Blessing of Many Fractures]]'', it is heavily implied that Joy Meachum hired Jessica Jones to find dirt on employees at Rand Enterprises. With the last time Jessica is seen before this being in ''[[AKA Smile]]'' on April 18, 2015, and this being said on February 21, 2016, it makes sense for her investigation to have been roughly in the middle of these two dates, around September 20, 2015.</ref>{{Ref|IF108}}
*[[Wilson Fisk]] is convicted on racketeering charges.{{Ref|DD311}}<ref>In ''[[Reunion (Daredevil)|Reunion]]'', on October 30, 2017 (see [[2017]] references), Benjamin Donovan states, "For the past two years, ever since his unjust conviction on racketeering charges, [Wilson Fisk] has maintained his innocence and fought to clear his good name." Taking a weighted calculation, this would suggest Fisk's conviction was around September 20, 2015. This fits well, as in ''[[The Man in the Box]]'', Fisk tells Matt Murdock, "We met once before, you and I. Before you went after me in court." This would mean that Fisk has already been convicted prior to the events of Season Two, which fits as being before October 27, 2015 (see other references). Additionally, at the end of ''[[Daredevil (episode)|Daredevil]]'', on December 16, 2014 (see [[2014]] references), Foggy Nelson estimates that getting a court date on Fisk's case "could take a year." Although Nelson's approximation has to be an overestimate whatever to the case, given Fisk states that only "several months" have passed since ''[[Speak of the Devil]]'' in ''[[The Man in the Box]]'', this places Fisk's court case around 8-9 months after the events of ''Daredevil'', significantly closer to a year than if it were only a few short months between seasons.</ref>
*Simmons watches her birthday messages video one last time, knowing that the NASA equipment will use the rest of her battery, then her and Daniels get to work setting up all the necessary equipment over the next few days.{{Ref|AoS305}}<ref name="4,722 Hours"/>

