====8th====
*A pre-release beta version of ''{{WPS|Star Wars Battlefront (2015 video game)|Star Wars Battlefront}}'' is released. The game would soon be frequently played by 14-year-old [[Alex Wilder]] and his friend, 16-year-old [[Amy Minoru]].{{Ref|RealEvents}}{{Ref|RW101}}

====11th====
*[[Alex Wilder]] and [[Amy Minoru]] are playing ''Star Wars Battlefront'' in [[Timely Coffee]], when Minoru complains that her laptop is running slow. Wilder runs a diagnosis and finds that her laptop has been hacked and is being key-logged. Minoru goes to look and is shocked and terrified when she realizes that the person behind it is her own mother: [[Tina Minoru]].<ref name="R1 2015 Sacrifice">''Star Wars: Battlefront'', which was released on November 17, 2015, was played by Amy Minoru in the days leading up to her death, suggesting she died no earlier than November 2015. However, in ''[[Hostile]]'', it is stated that the P.R.I.D.E. sacrifices are the "same time of year, every year", suggesting that the 2015 sacrifice, coinciding with Minoru's death, was almost exactly two years prior to October 13, 2017. Furthermore, when Wilder logs onto his PlayStation, it says that the last time Minoru played ''Star Wars: Battlefront'' was "2 years ago". The system for such operating systems is to round to the nearest integer below the exact number of years it has been, which means that "2 years ago" means between 2.000 and 2.999 years, and thus that Minoru played the game for the last time no later than October 13, 2015. Prior to the official release of ''Battlefront'', the game received an open beta release which was available from October 8-13, 2015. If Wilder and Minoru played the beta version of the game during this timeframe, this ends up fitting with Minoru's death being suggested to have been around October 2015.<br>
Prior to the Nico's discovery of Amy's body the morning following her death, Wizey tries to tell Amy that she will be late for school, meaning she died on a school night. Considering that the demo of ''Battlefront'' was only open from October 8-13 and Amy played the game at least two days prior to her death, she must have died anywhere between Sunday, October 11, 2015 and Thursday, October 15, 2015. It's generally implied throughout ''[[Reunion (Runaways)|Reunion]]'', based on the sadness looming over the Runaways throughout the episode and the fact that the two-year anniversary of Minoru's death is what ultimately reunites the characters, that it has been exactly two years since Minoru's death, so it can thus be taken that she died on October 13, 2015, with the flashbacks to the days leading up to her death dated to October 11, 2015 and October 12, 2015.</ref>{{Ref|RW108}}

